From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:07:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Platform layer: SDL3 audio, no busy wait, bigger zone

- i_sound.c: keep id's software mixer, but hand the 11025 Hz 16-bit
  stereo buffers to the platform layer (SDL3) instead of OSS /dev/dsp.
  Mix on demand while fewer than two buffers are queued, so audio is
  paced by the device instead of throttling the game. -nosound works.
- i_sound.c: linked sfx used a pointer difference divided by the struct
  size a second time.
- doomdef.h: no external sndserver; mix in-process.
- d_net.c: TryRunTics yields instead of spinning at 100% CPU.
- i_system.c: 32 MB zone for modern IWADs and PWADs.
---
 linuxdoom-1.10/d_net.c    |  2 +
 linuxdoom-1.10/doomdef.h  |  3 +-
 linuxdoom-1.10/i_sound.c  | 79 +++++++++++++--------------------------
 linuxdoom-1.10/i_system.c |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

